# Sounds Italian has not got, written for Urdu.
#
# The shape is Italian's own: a phoneme rule sets the source parameters and
# calls one locus rule for the place it is articulated at, where the formant
# targets are. What is here is the locus rules. Which phoneme reaches one is
# a call inside `ital_ph_<name>` in is_val.dr, changed there one line at a
# time, which is how lang/plpl does it too.

# The retroflex locus.
#
# A retroflex is a low third formant -- the tongue tip curled back lengthens
# the cavity in front of the constriction, and F3 comes down towards F2. That
# is the cue, and it is the one thing every description of the series agrees
# on.
#
# Italian's trill is f2 1250 and its dentals are f2 1700, both with a third
# formant left where the vowel had it. These numbers put F2 a little above
# the dentals and bring F3 down to meet it, which is the textbook retroflex
# and is deliberately not what Polish settled on: `pol_retroflex_Fv' is f2
# 1800 and f3 2500, a hair above Italian's palatal, because Polish sz is a
# palato-alveolar that its speakers hear as further back rather than a true
# retroflex. Urdu's are the real thing, so they start where the phonetics
# says and not where Polish's ear landed.
#
# Unheard as they stand. Polish's were arrived at by building three settings
# and listening to five words, and these have had no such hearing yet; when
# they get one this comment should say what was tried and what was kept.
rule urdu_retroflex_Fv takes 1 from is_val.obj
  call ZZfence_null
  set f2_in to 1750
  set f2_out to 1750
  set f3_in to 2100
  set f3_out to 2100
  match
end

# A neutral locus, for a sound made at the glottis.
#
# The place vocabulary runs lab, alv, pal, vel and ret, and none of those is
# the glottis: /h/ is made with the tract open and takes whatever shape the
# vowel beside it has. There is no way to say that here, so this is the
# middle of the mouth -- a neutral vowel's formants -- which is the nearest a
# fixed locus gets to one that has no place of its own.
rule urdu_glottal_Fv takes 1 from is_val.obj
  call ZZfence_null
  set f1_in to 500
  set f1_out to 500
  set f2_in to 1500
  set f2_out to 1500
  set f3_in to 2500
  set f3_out to 2500
  match
end

# /h/, which Italian has not got and Urdu leans on constantly: ہے and ہوں and
# every ہ in between were coming out as nothing at all.
#
# Written as ital_ph_s is -- the same two frication amplitudes and the same
# closing value -- and voiceless in the same way, which is by leaving out the
# store ital_ph_z makes and ital_ph_s does not: 2926, the voicing amplitude.
# That one word is the whole difference between the two in IBM's own rules,
# and it is what makes this breath rather than a buzz.
#
# It calls no locus rule, which is the point rather than an omission. /h/ has
# no place of its own: the tract is already in the shape of the vowel beside
# it and the breath passes through that shape. Setting a fixed locus made the
# formants jump to the middle of the mouth and back -- ہوں, which is /h/ then
# a back vowel, lurched audibly on the way in. Leaving them alone lets the
# neighbour's shape stand, which is what actually happens in a mouth.
# urdu_glottal_Fv is left above, unused, as the thing that was tried.
#
# It is reached by taking over L, Italian's gli, which no Urdu word wants.
# The call to it in ital_con_vals points here instead, and L's own record now
# says a voiceless fricative rather than a lateral.
rule urdu_ph_h takes 1 from is_val.obj
  call ZZfence_null
  set global half 2918 to 300
  set global half 2922 to 300
  set global half 2754 to 60
  match
end

# The retroflex stops, ٹ and ڈ, which Italian has not got and Urdu contrasts
# against its dentals in ordinary words: تال against ٹال, دال against ڈال.
#
# Written from ital_ph_t and ital_ph_d rather than invented. Those are three
# hundred and five hundred lines and most of it is context -- which locus to
# take before which neighbour -- so what is kept here is the part that makes
# the sound: the two frication amplitudes that are the burst, the locus, and
# the closing duration. The voiced one adds the store the voiceless one does
# not make, 2926, which is the same one word that separates ital_ph_s from
# ital_ph_z.
#
# The locus is urdu_retroflex_Fv, already written for ڑ: f2 1750 and f3 2100,
# a third formant brought down to meet the second, which is what a retroflex
# is. So the three retroflexes of Urdu now share one statement of where the
# tongue is, which is right -- they differ in manner and not in place.
#
# They are reached by taking over two Italian sounds no Urdu word wants: N,
# the gn of bagno, and Z, which Urdu writes as ژ and uses in perhaps a dozen
# borrowed words. That is the trade and it is worth stating: ژالہ will be
# said with a ڈ until there is somewhere else to put it.
rule urdu_ph_T takes 1 from is_val.obj
  call ZZfence_null
  set global half 2918 to 300
  set global half 2922 to 300
  call urdu_retroflex_Fv
  set global half 2918 to 500
  set global half 2858 to 55
  match
end

rule urdu_ph_D takes 1 from is_val.obj
  call ZZfence_null
  set global half 2918 to 200
  set global half 2922 to 200
  call urdu_retroflex_Fv
  set global half 2926 to 1000
  set global half 2858 to 55
  match
end
